WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.130
Lucía writes about a party:
Cuando llegué a la fiesta,

2
00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:05.650
Pablo había salido.

3
00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:09.410
One verb you know:
llegué, "I arrived".

4
00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:13.410
But this is a past you've
only glimpsed: había salido.

5
00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:16.110
Two past events, one sentence.

6
00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:20.810
So which came first: Lucía
arriving, or Pablo leaving?

7
00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:24.270
In this mission, you'll learn
to recognise the pluperfect:

8
00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:28.190
the imperfect of haber,
plus a past participle.

9
00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:30.590
Then you'll meet the imperative,

10
00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:34.870
the form behind orders on signs,
in recipes and in directions,

11
00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:36.970
like Gira a la derecha.

12
00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:40.510
You only need to understand
both, not produce them.

13
00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:42.930
Your mission: work out
which happened first,

14
00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:45.780
and decode every order you see.
